<===> README.md
Number literals are parsed in one go and correctly rounded like dart-sass
(composing integer, decimal and exponent parts accumulated rounding errors),
and large numbers are written from their shortest representation rounded
to the precision (`%.10f` showed digits beyond what a double can represent,
e.g. `6530020637.921538353`). Expected output generated with dart-sass
1.93.1.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> format/large_fraction/input.scss
a {
  b: 6530020637.921538353;
  c: 1234567.123456789123;
  d: -1234567.55555555555;
}
<===> format/large_fraction/output.css
a {
  b: 6530020637.921538;
  c: 1234567.1234567892;
  d: -1234567.5555555555;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> format/large_rounding/input.scss
a {
  b: 9999999.99999999999;
  c: -9999999.99999999999;
  d: 12345678.9;
}
<===> format/large_rounding/output.css
a {
  b: 10000000;
  c: -10000000;
  d: 12345678.9;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parse/beyond_2_53/input.scss
a {b: 9007199254740993}
<===> parse/beyond_2_53/output.css
a {
  b: 9007199254740992;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parse/exponent/input.scss
a {
  b: 1e300;
  c: 1.2345e20;
  d: 123.456e2;
}
<===> parse/exponent/output.css
a {
  b: ;
  c: 123450000000000000000;
  d: 12345.6;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parse/many_digits/input.scss
a {b: 123456789012345678}
<===> parse/many_digits/output.css
a {
  b: 123456789012345680;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parse/max_double/input.scss
a {b: 1.7976931348623157e308}
<===> parse/max_double/output.css
a {
  b: ;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> parse/small/input.scss
a {
  b: .5;
  c: +.5;
  d: 1e-7;
  e: -.25%;
}
<===> parse/small/output.css
a {
  b: 0.5;
  c: 0.5;
  d: 0.0000001;
  e: -0.25%;
}
